{
  "_comment": "Enemy preset curves, data-driven so retunes ride a restage instead of a rebuild. Two axes: crowdPoints (how busy fights are, snow's proven values) and rosterSteps (how scary the mix is, per-class weight multipliers over the catalog defaults in biorand_options.json). The five user-facing presets are curated pairs and reproduce the pre-split ladder exactly. Boss ratios are absolute values, not multipliers. hpPosition narrows every roster enemy's random-health band toward its floor (max' = min + t * (max - min)); boss-fight HP (boss-health-*) stays a free player dial. Design + evidence: ENEMY_CLASS_DESIGN.md at the repo root (untracked). Census: fork tools/enemy_census.py. classLock (Familiar/Varied, Cam 2026-08-16): at locked roster steps each spawn may only reroll within its vanilla occupant's class, so the threat map stays the designed campaign's while identity shuffles; classLockExempt classes stay eligible everywhere (the wandering cow rule). Wild and above roam free. vitalityPoints (2026-08-16, Cam): the HP band position is its own third dial; each pair pins the vitality that the old welding implied, so named presets are unchanged, and off-pair vitality expresses tanky-but-gentle or soft-but-apex runs.",
